<!--
  ⛔⛔⛔ A STIPULATION, NOT A FILING. See assets/fixtures/README.md. Nothing here was observed
  and nothing here may be cited as evidence about any business.

  ⭐⭐⭐ THE STATE THIS EXISTS FOR IS A SPREAD CONVERSION BENEATH A SPREAD CONVERSION. A
  composed layer's remainder is `F Phi r_parts`, each part's own remainder converted once, and
  a part that is ITSELF composed has a remainder of the same kind. So the definition recurses,
  and it bottoms out at a leaf where `n` and `d` are independently filed.

  ⛔⛔ EVERY OTHER NESTED CHAIN IN THIS REPOSITORY BOTTOMS OUT AT DEPTH ONE BY ACCIDENT, because
  no part that is itself composed also carries a factor with WIDTH. Where the factor is a point
  the two readings of a part's remainder coincide, so reading the part's own `n - d` in place of
  its converted remainder costs nothing and the recursion is invisible. This document is the one
  where it is not.

  ⭐⭐ THE CHAIN, AND BOTH EDGES HAVE WIDTH:

      line-runs  =[0.8, 1.0, 1.25]=>  line-hours  =[0.5, 1.0, 2.0]=>  line-batches

  A run does not take a fixed time and a batch does not take a fixed number of hours, so
  neither factor can be filed as a point without asserting a precision the line does not have.

  ⭐⭐⭐ THE THREE ANSWERS, AND ONLY ONE IS THE REMAINDER:

      line-runs        n = 10, d = 8            r = [2, 2, 2]

      line-hours       n - d differenced        [-2.0, 2, 6.1]
                       0.8 . r_runs converted   [ 1.6, 2, 2.5]     <- the remainder

      line-batches     n - d differenced        [-16.0, 2, 21.8]
                       converted from the       [ -4.0, 2, 12.2]   <- reads line-hours WRONG
                         DIFFERENCED line-hours
                       converted from the       [  0.8, 2,  5.0]   <- the remainder
                         CONVERTED line-hours

  ⛔ The middle figure is what a one-level pivot returns. It is not a rounding difference from
  the third: `line-hours` differenced straddles zero and converted does not, so the corner rule
  reads opposite ends of the factor and the two answers are five units apart at the low bound.

  ⚠️ THE FILED SHARES ARE THE THIRD FIGURE, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THIS DOCUMENT A TEST RATHER
  THAN AN ILLUSTRATION. `checks/shares_do_not_sum` compares a holder's share against the
  magnitude of `r`, so a reader computing `line-batches` one level deep accuses this filing,
  and a reader computing it by recursion does not. The document is correct either way; only one
  of the two readings agrees with it.
-->
